# ── Trained model artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELIBERATE DECISION, documented because the previous .gitignore contradicted
# itself: it excluded backend/ml/models/ and *.pt while two checkpoints were
# committed anyway.
#
# Every trained artifact IS committed. Together they are about 1 MB, and
# shipping them is what makes `docker compose up` produce a working demo with
# real models instead of silent heuristic fallbacks — which was the single worst
# defect in this project's history. Reproduce them from scratch with
# `make train` (~35 min on a laptop CPU, no GPU required).
ml/checkpoints/checkpoints_rl/
ml/logs/

# ── Generated artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benchmark results ARE committed so the dashboard's report panel works on a
# fresh clone and the honesty gates have something to check. Regenerate with
# `make bench`.
experiments/runs/
experiments/report_assets/
!experiments/results/

# Data artifacts
datasets/raw/
datasets/processed/
*.db
